                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The unknown-verb error message still says '(expected bind, record or verify)' although 'check' is now a valid verb, so the user-facing message is stale. This is a minor accuracy issue, not a security risk.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/cmd/review.go:59-62"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "deterministic",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed the full diff of engine/cmd/review.go and engine/cmd/review_check_test.go for security, authorization, data exposure, unsafe input handling and secrets.",
              "The new check verb is read-only: it stores nothing, and the tests assert that the results directory is unchanged after both cleared and refused checks.",
              "The --head value is validated by the service before git reads it: the test at engine/cmd/review_check_test.go covers a head starting with '-' being refused so git cannot read it as an option, and checks that no file is written. The Check implementation itself is outside this candidate, so this is only verified through the tests.",
              "The --head flag handling distinguishes a given empty value from the default through the new given map, so an explicit empty head is refused rather than silently falling back to HEAD. This avoids a case where an explicit option is silently ignored.",
              "The check verb prints only head, base, digest and stored file names, so no secrets or sensitive data are exposed.",
              "The only issue found is the stale unknown-verb message, which does not affect security. The line I cited (engine/cmd/review.go:62) is not a line this candidate changed, so the finding's introduced disposition is inaccurate and the issue is effectively pre-existing wording that the new verb has made stale."
            ]
          }
        }
