              {
                "id": "R3-001",
                "lens": "reliability",
                "location": "engine/cmd/review.go:59",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The new 'check' verb is dispatched, but the unchanged default branch still reports the unknown-verb error as 'expected bind, record or verify'. A user who mistypes a verb is not told that check exists. This is a stale message, not a failure of the new verb, and no test asserts it.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/cmd/review.go:59"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed the full patch of both manifest paths, engine/cmd/review.go and engine/cmd/review_check_test.go.",
              "The head-flag handling is sound. An explicit empty --head is rejected through the given map and require, and HEAD is the default only when the flag is absent. That behavior is a deliberate design choice, but no test passes an empty --head, so it is unproved.",
              "The check tests cover the clear, verdict with fix and carry, and refusal paths. The refusals cover never reviewed, another head, another feature, blocked, unchecked severe finding, tampered digest, and an invalid stored file. They also cover a non-commit head, an option-like head, and --cwd resolution. Each asserts stdout, stderr, exit code and that nothing is stored, so the candidate behavior is largely proved.",
              "Failure paths exit 1 with a single stderr line and empty stdout. The failure to write stdout after clearing is handled in reportChecked, but no test exercises it.",
              "I could not check the helpers the tests use (newReviewWorld, recordBlocker, verdictOn, listNames), because they are outside this candidate. I also could not check that the given map in parseReviewFlags is keyed by the flag text. The has method relies on that, and the visible hunk does not show it."
            ]
          }
        }
